<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00KT">Remark <span data-tag="00KT">2.4.3.6</span>.</a> The homotopy coherent nerve $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ was introduced by Cordier in <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/MR648798">MR648798</a>]</span> (motivated by earlier work of Vogt on the theory of homotopy coherence; see <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/MR0331376">MR0331376</a>]</span>). Beware that Cordier uses slightly different conventions: <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/MR648798">MR648798</a>]</span> defines the homotopy coherent nerve of a simplicial category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ to be the simplicial set $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{c}} )$, where $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{c}}$ denotes the <em>conjugate</em> of the simplicial category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ (Example <a data-tag="00KE" href="/tag/00KE">2.4.2.12</a>). </p>
</article>
